  title={A 24.5–45.2-GHz Low-Jitter Compact Differentially Injection-Locked Clock Multiplier With Folded-Inductor-Based Magnetic-Flux Cancellation},
  year={2026},
  volume={61},
  number={4},
  pages={1410-1424},
  abstract={In this article, we present a differentially injection-locked clock multiplier (ILCM) featuring an ultra-wide frequency tuning range (TR) and low jitter, achieved through a compact folded-inductor-based magnetic-flux cancellation technique. A co-designed series-LC dual-mode quadrature ring oscillator (QRO) and edge-combining frequency doubler operating in the mm-wave band jointly extend the TR while suppressing phase noise (PN). Furthermore, a differential time-aligning technique enables an exceptionally wide loop bandwidth ( $f_{\text {BW}}$ ). Fabricated in 28-nm HPC+ CMOS, the prototype QRO exhibits a 59.46% TR (12.25–22.6 GHz), while the doubler output spans 24.5–45.23 GHz. Despite its compact core area of 0.037 mm2, the ILCM achieves an rms jitter of 32.83 fs at 39.5 GHz.},
